# Kraken2 pipeline data — lives on Setonix scratch (~200GB: CDS downloads, BUSCO
# lineage caches, Kraken2 DBs, downloaded FASTQ). Ignore the data by exact subdir
# name (small tracked TSVs — ref_candidates.tsv, busco_scores.tsv, manifest.tsv —
# live alongside these in the same data/ dirs and stay tracked). manifest.tsv
# (generated by manifest.py, at repo root) records what exists remotely without
# holding the data itself. See memory/kraken_restructure_plan.md.
# Paths updated 2026-09-25 for the flattened module/<step>/ layout (kraken/db/search
# -> 03_kraken/01_search, kraken/db/utilities -> 03_kraken/utilities, etc.). The four kraken/db/
# entries below were missed when the structure moved and left the Setonix data dirs
# unignored; db_v3 added at the same time. kraken_run_download/ dropped entirely.
03_kraken/01_search/data/cds/
03_kraken/utilities/busco/data/busco_downloads/
03_kraken/utilities/busco/data/busco_scan_cache.tsv
03_kraken/02_build/data/db_v2/
03_kraken/02_build/data/db_v3/
03_kraken/02_build/data/db/
03_kraken/03_select/data/reads/
03_kraken/utilities/split/data/index/
03_kraken/utilities/split/data/reads/
03_kraken/utilities/split/data/_tmp/

# FracMinHash sketch cache — one .npy per assembly (~700 MB on Setonix), the only
# expensive part of kraken_db_saturation.py and fully rebuilt by --stage sketch.
# The curve/bias/policy stages read it and write the small TSVs, which stay tracked.
03_kraken/utilities/saturation/data/sketches/

# Stray SLURM .out/.err that older kraken scripts dropped at the repo root on
# Setonix before every --output path pointed at 03_kraken/slurm/logs/.
/*.out
/*.err

# Ensembl Plants REST species list — cache for kraken_hosts.py geo lookups, refetched
# if absent, not needed on Setonix (which downloads via --from-table). The ignore here
# pointed at the pre-flatten path and so never applied; the file is now tracked at
# 03_kraken/01_search/data/ensembl_species.json (84 KB). Left tracked deliberately — untrack
# with `git rm --cached` if the cache should stay local-only.

# Personal reference/prose: pipeline schematic, literature notes, manuscript drafts.
# Kept on disk for navigation, not version-controlled (Leon's call 2026-09-24).
# docs/ holds drafts, the manuscript and collaborators' material: all local.
# The pipeline schematic is the exception - it is documentation a reader of the repo
# needs, so it is tracked.
docs/*
!docs/pipeline_schematic.md

# 03_kraken/05_filter: large regeneratable data tables (rebuilt by detect.py / prep_*.py from
# 03_kraken/04_assign/data/reports, itself gitignored). Small manifests with no generator
# (model2d.tsv, slopes_*, graminis_*, fsp_*) stay tracked; scripts + figures stay tracked.
03_kraken/05_filter/data/_classified.tsv
03_kraken/05_filter/data/complexity_byhost.tsv
03_kraken/05_filter/data/three.tsv
03_kraken/05_filter/data/splitfig.tsv
# _scratch holds superseded exploratory versions, kept on disk for local reference
# only (same treatment as legacy/): excluded from the repo entirely.
03_kraken/05_filter/_scratch/

# 04_kallisto: the large, Setonix-built outputs only. The small step outputs that ARE the
# record stay tracked: 01_select/data/strata.tsv (the calibration set, deterministic but the
# definition of the experiment) and 02_build/data/neighbours.tsv (the containment measurement,
# cheap to recompute but only from sketches that live on scratch under a purge).
04_kallisto/02_build/data/idx/
04_kallisto/03_quant/data/*
!04_kallisto/03_quant/data/.gitkeep
04_kallisto/04_confirm/data/*
!04_kallisto/04_confirm/data/.gitkeep

