03_kraken/02_build/data/db_v3_summary.txt
03_kraken/03_select/data/run_list.tsv
03_kraken/03_select/data/spots.tsv
03_kraken/03_select/data/verify*.tsv
03_kraken/03_select/data/host_taxid_to_accession.json
03_kraken/04_assign/data/classify_smoke/
03_kraken/04_assign/smoke_ram/
03_kraken/04_assign/smoke_mmap/

# One pathological SLURM log: the retired backup_dbv3.slurm retried a hard S3 refusal in
# a tight loop and produced 13.8 MB of identical errors. The failure is understood (wrong
# Acacia allocation, see the Acacia note) and the file would otherwise need a history
# rewrite to remove. Kept on disk on Setonix, out of git.
03_kraken/slurm/logs/acacia_dbv3_49970753.err

# Provenance enrichment (2026-10-02), same code-not-data rule. The supplements are
# publishers' copyrighted supplementary files, not ours to redistribute; the rest are
# regeneratable from them plus the caches (ENA accession resolution, Nominatim geocodes).
02_literature/02_text/data/supp_data/
02_literature/02_text/data/supp_accession_map.json
02_literature/02_text/data/supp_provenance.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/cohort_provenance.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/provenance_tracker.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/country_summary.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/localities.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/localities_plot.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/geocode_cache.json

# 01a_Literature: search returns and resolved accession lists. Data, per the code-not-data
# policy; the prompts that produced them are tracked and are the reproducible part.
01a_Literature/data/*
!01a_Literature/data/.gitkeep

# The hand-built records used to live here as exceptions to the rule above, which meant
# tracking depended on whether somebody remembered `git add -f`: joins.tsv was never added to
# the list and three generated tables were force-added by mistake. They now live in
# 01a_Literature/seeds/, which is OUTSIDE this rule and therefore tracked by default, and
# 01a_Literature/gold/ holds the small human-readable outputs. See 01a_Literature/_paths.py.
#
#   seeds/  HAND-WRITTEN, irreplaceable, tracked. Losing it costs re-reading every paper.
#   gold/   generated but tiny and worth having in history: summary numbers over time.
#   data/   generated tables, ignored. Losing it costs a refetch and nothing else.
#   bronze/ immutable external captures (runinfo, BioSample attrs, GEO, ENA), ignored.
01a_Literature/bronze/**

# 01a_Literature working files. studies/ is the manual drop zone and holds publisher PDFs and
# supplementary spreadsheets, which are not ours to redistribute (same grounds as
# 02_literature/02_text/data/manual_pdfs/). The adapters ARE the reproducible part and are
# tracked; so are the Undermind reports and the prompts.
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so re-including a file inside one needs the
# directories re-included at every level first. `studies/*` alone would hide the adapters.
01a_Literature/studies/**
!01a_Literature/studies/*/
!01a_Literature/studies/*/adapter.yaml
01a_Literature/*.pdf
01a_Literature/*.xls
01a_Literature/*.xlsx

# WSL writes an alternate-data-stream sidecar next to anything downloaded through Windows.
# Pure noise, never ours, and they appear beside every PDF and spreadsheet dropped into
# 01a_Literature/studies/.
*:Zone.Identifier
